================================================================================
## Port Graph Chat performance work onto 0.9.0
================================================================================

Context:
The Graph Chat accuracy / latency work landed on the 0.8.1 line
(feat/graph-chat-performance, changelogs/v0.8.1/simyung-yang_data_2026-10-12,
-10-14 and -10-15). 0.9.0 has no shared history with that line, so the work is
re-applied here as a 3-way patch and reconciled with 0.9.0's own changes:
companion-table reads (_adj_in / _adj_out / _entity_search / _props),
single-statement Explorer expand, GraphFilter, per-tool tracing,
require_read_only_sparql, and the architecture guardrails (one public class
per file, 800-LOC class / 100-LOC function budgets).

Policy: 0.9.0 wins for BFS / expand / companion reads; GraphQL filters,
counts and inverse fields, analyze_graphql, the schema digest, tool-result
compaction and the prompt rules are added on top. The old Explorer edge
pruning is re-implemented on GraphFilter instead of DigitalTwin.

Changes:

1. src/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/engine.py, tools.py, analysis.py,
   AnalysisError.py, EntityRef.py
   Schema digest in the system prompt, analyze_graphql (exact server-side
   group / intersect / difference / union), compaction of older tool results,
   CHAT_MAX_TOKENS (ONTOBRICKS_CHAT_MAX_TOKENS, default 8192), unreadable
   reply logging, drop_unresolvable_links on the final reply. The tool-call
   loop moved to _run_tool_calls so run_agent stays within its size budget.
   AnalysisError and EntityRef got their own files (one class per file).
2. src/agents/tracing.py
   Tool spans record result length and status, plus payloads when
   trace_payloads_enabled(). The trace_tool decorator was not re-added to
   engine_base.dispatch_tool: 0.9.0 already traces each tool, and both
   together produced duplicate TOOL spans.
3. src/back/core/graphdb/SubjectFilter.py, SubjectFilterKind.py,
   SubjectQueryMixin.py, GraphDBBackend.py
   Typed-subject filters, count_subjects_by_type (with distinct_predicate)
   and find_subjects_by_predicate_objects live in SubjectQueryMixin, mixed
   into GraphDBBackend. find_subjects_by_type uses the entity-search
   companion only when no filters are given.
4. src/back/core/graphdb/neo4j/Neo4jSubjectQueryMixin.py, Neo4jReadOps.py,
   Neo4jStore.py
   Native-Cypher counterparts in Neo4jSubjectQueryMixin, mixed into
   Neo4jReadOps (keeps the class under 800 LOC).
5. src/back/core/graphql/* (FieldFilter, InverseField, InverseSource,
   RelEdge, RelTarget, SchemaDigest, SchemaMetadata, GraphQLSchemaBuilder,
   ResolverFactory, models, constants)
   GraphQL list filters, <list>Count, inverse <plural>Via<Property> fields,
   selection-aware loading, schema digest (12000-char cap, attributes kept
   before levels are dropped, warning logs). models.py now holds only
   TypeInfo; the other records got their own files.
6. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinChatDigest.py, __init__.py,
   src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py
   TwinChatDigest.build(domain, domain_name) builds the chat schema digest
   (kept out of DigitalTwin, which is at its class budget). Both chat routes
   pass schema_digest; _chat_forwarded_headers is shared by both routes.
   0.9.0's GraphFilter.clamp_max_entities replaces the old FILTER_* constants.
7. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/explorer/GraphFilter.py, DigitalTwin.py
   GraphFilter.bounded_expand wraps expand (both the single-statement and
   BFS paths) and drops relationship triples whose object is outside the
   expanded set (drop_out_of_set_edges), so max_entities bounds what the
   Explorer draws. DigitalTwin.filter_expand calls it.
8. src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js
   Explorer focus / centring fixes kept; DEFAULT_MAX_ENTITIES = 5000 to match
   GraphFilter.EXPLORER_MAX_ENTITIES_DEFAULT and the 0.9.0 template.
9. src/back/core/graphdb/constants.py, lakebase/_companion_ddl.py,
   src/agents/tools/graph_formatting.py
   REVERSE_LOOKUP_MAX_ROWS, reverse-edge index DDL, KRW formatting.
10. Tests: test_agent_dtwin_chat_analysis.py, test_graphql_relationship_queries.py,
    test_graph_store_subject_filters.py, test_neo4j_subject_filters.py,
    test_filter_expand_bounds.py (incl. the single-statement expand path),
    test_graph_formatting_krw.py; updated engine / tracing / lakebase tests.
11. .planning/agents/agent_dtwin_chat/SPEC.md,
    tests/eval/datasets/agent_dtwin_chat/regression.jsonl
    SPEC and regression dataset for the new tools.

