================================================================================
## Restore app self-permissions before the apps start
================================================================================

Context:
`databricks bundle deploy` rewrites the app ACL from databricks.yml
`permissions:` and drops the app service principal's CAN_MANAGE on its own app
(and the MCP SP's CAN_USE on the main app). deploy.sh only restored them after
`bundle run`, so anyone opening the freshly restarted app hit
/access-denied?reason=bootstrap until step 10 finished. Ported from the 0.8.1
line (feat/graph-chat-performance 8387f8a3).

Changes:

1. scripts/deploy.sh
   New step 6c "App self-permissions (pre-start)" runs
   scripts/bootstrap/app-permissions.sh "$APP_NAME" "$MCP_APP_NAME" after
   `bundle deploy` and the 6b synced-source re-deploy, before step 8 starts
   the apps. Gated on --no-bootstrap like step 10; a failure only warns.
   Step 10 is kept as an idempotent backstop; both share
   grant_app_self_permissions(). --help range follows the longer header.
2. tests/units/scripts/test_deploy_app_permissions_prestart.py
   Wiring (after the last bundle deploy, before bundle run, honours
   --no-bootstrap, backstop kept) and the real helper run against a fake
   bootstrap script (passes both app names, failure warns and continues).

Modified files:
- scripts/deploy.sh
- tests/units/scripts/test_deploy_app_permissions_prestart.py
- changelogs/v0.9.0/simyung-yang_2026-10-19.log

Tests: `bash -n scripts/deploy.sh` OK (shellcheck not installed).
`.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/units/scripts tests/units/settings tests/units/architecture`
-> 1045 passed. The new test file fails 7/7 against origin/0.9.0's deploy.sh.
Not deployed.
